    remove 3 from ages
           ^

Line 15: All the keys of a map have to be the same kind: the first is text, but this is a number.
    let mixed be a map of "a" to 1, 2 to 3
                                    ^

Line 16: All the values of a map have to be the same kind: the first is a number, but this is text.
    let mixed values be a map of "a" to 1, "b" to "two"
                                                  ^^^^^

Line 17: A map's keys have to be text or numbers, but this is a yes/no value.
    let flags be a map of yes to 1
                          ^^^

Line 18: The key "tea" is in this map twice.
    let twice be a map of "tea" to 2, "tea" to 3
                                      ^^^^^
Each key has one value, so give each key once.

Line 19: The key 1 is in this map twice.
    let twice numbers be a map of 1 to 2, 1.0 to 3
                                          ^^^
Each key has one value, so give each key once.

Line 20: A map has a key and a value in each entry, so going through it takes two names.
    for each name in ages:
                     ^^^^
Name both, like "for each name and age in ages:". To go through only the keys, write "for each name in the keys of ages:".

Line 22: A "for each" loop with two names needs a map to go through, but this is a list of numbers.
    for each a1 and b1 in scores:
                          ^^^^^^
A list has one item at a time, so name it once, like "for each score in scores:".

Line 24: I can only set a value in a map, but this is a list of numbers.
    set the value for "x" in scores to 1
                             ^^^^^^
To change an item of a list, write "set item 2 of scores to ...".

