    say ages contains "Paris"
        ^^^^
To check whether a map has a key, use "has".

Line 34: This value is a list of numbers, so this could mean two things.
    add 5 to the value for "a" in graph
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
To put it at the end of the list, write "add ... to the end of the value for ...". To add it to every item, set the value to "every n in ... plus ...".

Line 35: This value is a list of numbers, so this could mean two things.
    add "x" to the value for "a" in graph
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
To put it at the end of the list, write "add ... to the end of the value for ...". To add it to every item, set the value to "every n in ... plus ...".

Line 36: "ages" is a map from text to numbers (made on line 2), but this is a map from text to lists of numbers.
    set ages to graph
                ^^^^^
A variable keeps the kind of value it was made with. To keep a map from text to lists of numbers, make a new variable for it.

